# Documented escape hatch for Trivy image scanning.
#
# The CI gate fails the build on any HIGH/CRITICAL vulnerability in the image
# (application dependencies + the Chainguard base). Chainguard is continuously
# rebuilt to carry ~zero known CVEs, so this should stay empty. If an
# unavoidable HIGH/CRITICAL ever appears before an upstream rebuild lands, add
# its CVE id below (one per line) with a comment explaining why and a review
# date, e.g.:
#
#   CVE-2025-XXXXX  # base image; awaiting Chainguard rebuild; re-check 2026-01-01
#
# Keep this file empty by default — every entry is a knowingly accepted risk.
